# Keep the Docker build context small and, critically, exclude the host build
# tree (which may contain macOS artifacts that would collide with the in-container
# `-B build` configure). vcpkg is cloned inside the image, so the repo .git is
# not needed either.
# Exclude every host build directory (build/, build-linux/, build-debug/,
# build-release/, ...) plus CLion's cmake-build-* trees, which `build*/` does
# not match. The container configures its own ./build internally; copying host
# build trees in both bloats the context and can fill the VM disk (a 1.3 GB
# cmake-build-debug/ was seen doing exactly that).
build*/
cmake-build-*/
.git/
_artifacts/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
clients/macos/**/build/
clients/macos/**/DerivedData/
clients/beebium-typescript-client/dist/
vcpkg_installed/
*.tgz
